<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/central-venous-catheters> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Central Venous Catheters" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "文档中指出使用中心静脉导管可能增加静脉血栓栓塞的风险，属于可干预因素。" ;
    dmo:name "Central Venous Catheters" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Modifiable" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "central-venous-catheters" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Several other complications may occur with some being relatively common, generally mild and easily treated. However, others may be more serious. These include the development of venous thromboembolic disease, particularly if central venous catheters are used." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_dka_guideline_with_qr_code_march_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/eating-disorders> a dmo:RiskFactor ;
    rdfs:label "Eating Disorders" ;
    dmo:evidenceNote "For those with recurrent admissions, there is often a psychological element (e.g. eating disorders, other undiagnosed mental health disorders), that is likely to benefit from formal mental health team involvement" ;
    dmo:name "Eating Disorders" ;
    dmo:riskCategory "Obstetric" ;
    dmo:riskFactorCode "eating-disorders" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For those with recurrent admissions, there is often a psychological element (e.g. eating disorders, other undiagnosed mental health disorders), that is likely to benefit from formal mental health team involvement" ;
